## Patch 5 — Required tests

1. `PUT /api/age-assurance` accepts only `13_15`, `16_17`, or `18_plus` with `attested:true`.
2. `GET /api/age-assurance` never returns `users.date_of_birth`.
3. Directly setting `ageBand=18_plus` in a Kinfolk request body does nothing; the server reads the table only.
4. A 13–15 account asking general Black maternal health questions gets simple evidence-backed education, source labels, safety boundary, and `Show more`.
5. The same 13–15 account requesting deep detail gets deeper non-graphic evidence context, not adult/graphic content.
6. A pregnancy/postpartum emergency-symptom prompt invokes the emergency path before a long answer at every band.
7. An unknown age band uses protective delivery and cannot retrieve adult/graphic community media.
8. A 13–15 user can read Muslim/Christmas and interracial-relationship Library topics with respectful, non-stereotyped delivery.
9. Profile, session payload, community API, business dashboard, Kinfolk logs, and vectors do not expose DOB.
10. The 30-session canary passes after age code is added, using clean bundle identity and member-keyed rate limits.

